<title>USA: US banks free reserves $738 mln Sept 25 rvsd 2 wks.</title>
<headline>US banks free reserves $738 mln Sept 25 rvsd 2 wks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $738 million per day in the revised two weeks ended September 25, versus revised free reserves of $574 million in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $317 million versus $308 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
